    "FineTuningData": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Private material the resume carries for a tailoring run.\n\nA top-level section rather than a corner of `basics`, because none of it is\nresume content: it is what shapes the selection and the wording, and it is\nnever rendered. It holds no contact details \u2014 those are official fields of\n`basics` now, and the MCP client reads the whole private document, so\nrestating them here would only create a second copy to keep in step.\n\nThe rules for a tailoring run live in `ResumeSkill`, not here. What belongs\nhere is what is about *this person* rather than about the procedure.",
      "properties": {
        "narrative": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Narrative"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "logistics": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/Logistics"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        }
      },
      "title": "FineTuningData",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Highlight": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One accomplishment. A string officially; an object here.\n\nThe schema's `highlights[]` is a list of finished bullets. This is the\nmaterial a bullet is written from: `summary` is the bullet itself, and the\nrest is what tailoring needs to decide whether the bullet belongs in *this*\ndocument and how to word it for *this* posting.",
      "properties": {
        "publish": {
          "default": true,
          "description": "False withholds this entry from the public feed only. It has no bearing on a tailored resume or cover letter: an entry withheld from a published website is often exactly the one to lead with in an application. Absent means published.",
